  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'slow travel' is gaining popularity among tourists who want to experience the authentic culture and beauty of a place without contributing to its degradation. Slow travel involves staying in one location for an extended period, often using public transportation or walking, and engaging with the local community.\n\nThis approach not only reduces carbon emissions but also allows visitors to appreciate the nuances of the destination's history, architecture, and way of life. For instance, a traveler who stays in a small town in rural Italy might visit local markets, attend village festivals, and participate in traditional cooking classes.\n\nIn contrast, mass tourism can have devastating effects on the environment and local communities. The influx of large numbers of tourists can lead to overcrowding, pollution, and strain on resources such as water and energy. Furthermore, the commercialization of tourist areas can erase the unique character of a place, replacing it with generic amenities and services that cater to the needs of visitors rather than locals.\n\nAs the world becomes increasingly interconnected, slow travel offers a refreshing alternative to the traditional tourist experience. By adopting this approach, travelers can not only reduce their environmental footprint but also gain a deeper understanding and appreciation of the cultures they visit.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article about slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It's a way to see many places in a short time.\", \"It involves staying in one location for an extended period and engaging with the local community.\", \"It's only suitable for people who have a lot of money.\", \"It's not environmentally friendly.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is likely to happen if many tourists visit a small town in rural Italy?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The town will become more prosperous and beautiful.\", \"The local community will be able to provide more services for visitors.\", \"Overcrowding, pollution, and strain on resources are possible outcomes.\", \"The town's unique character will remain unchanged.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the author mean by 'commercialization of tourist areas'?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The replacement of local businesses with international chain stores.\", \"The development of new infrastructure to cater to tourists.\", \"The loss of unique character and charm in a place due to mass tourism.\", \"The increase in prices for locals due to tourism.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards traditional tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Positive, as it brings economic benefits and creates jobs.\", \"Negative, as it has devastating effects on the environment and local communities.\", \"Neutral, as it depends on individual circumstances.\", \"Ambivalent, as it has both positive and negative aspects.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is a potential advantage of slow travel for travelers?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They can visit many places in a short time.\", \"They can gain a deeper understanding and appreciation of the cultures they visit.\", \"They can save money by staying in hostels and eating at street food stalls.\", \"They can reduce their environmental footprint.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
